Chapter: VecLanePastEnd
  cites Foreword chapter Console

 `vec-extract` takes a `Vector 2`, so lanes 0 and 1 exist and lane 2 does
 not. The lane count is fixed by the builtin's own type, so this is decided
 at CHECK and the binary is never emitted.

 The negative half of the same guard is in
 codex/test/errors/vec-lane-negative.codex, and the two are separate files
 because they fail for different reasons: one compares against the lane
 count and one against zero. A single test naming CDX2093 would pass with
 half the check reverted.

 The positive control is codex/test/ops/vec-lanes-smoke.codex, which reads
 both legal lanes and a COMPUTED lane, and codex/test/vector-f32.codex,
 which reads lane 3 of a `Vector 4` through vec4-extract -- the last legal
 lane, which a check written with the wrong comparison would refuse.

Section: Entry

  opening : [Console] Nothing = act
    print-line-uni (show (vec-extract (vec-splat 1.5) 2))
  end

